      "sequence_position": 19,
      "problem": "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<2 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}-4}{21}, & 2\\le x\\le 5 \\\\ 1, & x>5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(3<X<4).$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that for continuous random variables, it doesn't matter whether or not we include the endpoints of the interval. So we can perform this computation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3<X<4) & =P(3<X\\le 4) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 4)-P(X\\le 3) \\\\  & =F(4)-F(3) \\\\  & =\\frac{{4}^{2}-4}{21}-\\frac{{3}^{2}-4}{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
